1. The "Day 0" Reality (1 Minute)
Slide Idea: A simple flowchart: User → Frontend → Backend → OpenAI API.

The Pitch: "Most AI projects start as a simple wrapper. It’s fast to build, but it’s a 'black box.' We have no control over costs, no visibility into what users are asking, and our secrets (API keys) are scattered across the backend."

2. The "Day 1" Challenges (2 Minutes)
The Problem: Explain that as you scale, you hit four walls:

Security: APIs are exposed to the public internet; keys are in environment variables.

Cost: You’re paying for the same "summarize this text" call 1,000 times because there's no cache.

Fragmentation: Marketing uses ChatGPT, Devs use Gemini, and the business wants to use Copilot—nothing is unified.

Brittle Logic: The app can't "do" anything; it can only "chat."

3. The Solution: The Agentic Enterprise Architecture (3 Minutes)
Slide Idea: Show the last diagram I generated for you.

Key Highlights:

The VNET "Moat": Everything is tucked inside a private network. No public endpoints for the database or backend.

The AI Gateway (APIM): This is your control tower. It handles caching (saving money), observability (who is using what?), and security (identity-based access).

Multi-Model Strategy: We aren't locked into OpenAI. We can swap to Gemini or use Apify for web data seamlessly through the same gateway.

4. Justifying the "Agentic" Shift (2 Minutes)
The Pitch: "We aren't just building a chatbot; we're building an Agentic System."

Why Microsoft Agent Framework? Because it allows the app to use Tools.

If the user asks about a website, the agent calls Apify.

If the user wants a workflow in Copilot Studio, the APIs are already registered and ready.

The Managed Agent Service handles the "memory" so the agent remembers the user across sessions without us writing custom database logic every time.

5. The "Bottom Line" (ROI) (2 Minutes)
Security: Zero Trust architecture.

Reusability: Build an API once in Azure, and use it in your Custom App and Copilot Studio.

Observability: One dashboard to see the cost of every single token across all models.

Future-Proof: The Agent Framework means we can add "skills" to the AI without rewriting the core architecture.
